framework DecisionAudit

domain Issue21RequirementIndependentReview:
  description "Independent review of Plan Review Request Requirements Candidate 1.0"

problem P1:
  "Is exact candidate a43466a2922d10795e0c6696e2eb1336d2e7ac0005a519ce2604c691eb94e132 internally consistent with Issue 21 and the current Grammar 9, CLI Contract 10, governance, assurance, acceptance, recommendation, and history authorities?"

step S1:
  premise PR1:
    "The selected REVIEW_THEN_DECIDE route in docs/process/issue-21-requirement-review-input.md requires review of the unchanged candidate and review input, classification of every material result, and return to a second owner decision without editing or accepting the requirement"

step S2:
  evidence EV1:
    "Product-source GitHub Issue 21 requests a persistent machine-readable advisory before new downstream work, keeps task eligibility and start authority unchanged, separates request creation and resolution from plan-change authority, leaves exact DSL and schema to design, and does not authorize implementation"

step S3:
  evidence EV2:
    "Exact candidate docs/requirements/plan-review-request-v1.md identifies Grammar 9 and CLI Contract 10 as the current authority, proposes additive Grammar 10 and Contract 11, requires explicit request identity and time, makes review advisory-only, preserves existing governance and assurance boundaries, and excludes implementation and publication"

step S4:
  evidence EV3:
    "Candidate docs/requirements/plan-review-request-v1.md section 4 says resolving a request clears the project-wide review-required advisory, while section 5 derives review_required whenever at least one request remains open and the acceptance criteria require multiple-open-request coverage"

step S5:
  decision D1 based_on EV3:
    "There is a high-severity internal contradiction from candidate authoring: resolving one request cannot clear the project-wide advisory when another request remains open"

step S6:
  evidence EV4:
    "Candidate docs/requirements/plan-review-request-v1.md sections 2 and 6 propose replacement Perttool.NextResult.v9 for Contract 11, while section 9 says Grammar 1 through 9 inputs retain their exact current result identities; docs/specs/json-schema.md identifies the current result as Perttool.NextResult.v8"

step S7:
  decision D2 based_on EV4:
    "There is a high-severity compatibility contradiction from candidate authoring unless the requirement explicitly chooses either version-dispatched v8 results for legacy inputs or v9 results with preserved legacy semantics but a changed envelope identity"

step S8:
  evidence EV5:
    "Candidate docs/requirements/plan-review-request-v1.md permits plan_changed resolution without performing or authorizing a plan mutation, records only the reviewed pre-resolution source digest, and does not define whether plan_changed means a review decision to change or evidence that a separately governed change already occurred"

step S9:
  decision D3 based_on EV5:
    "The meaning and evidence binding of plan_changed is a medium-severity unresolved unknown for the later contract; it is not established as a contradiction because the candidate can define it as a review conclusion rather than a completed mutation"

step S10:
  evidence EV6:
    "Current docs/specs/governance-authority.md derives affected goal and DAG scopes from candidate changes and treats owner assertions as candidate-bound caller assertions, while Candidate 1.0 proposes operation-specific resolution authority without classifying the request resolution as a DAG mutation"

step S11:
  decision D4 based_on EV6:
    "The exact result shape and diagnostic behavior for operation-specific resolution authority is a medium-severity contract unknown, not a current-authority contradiction, because the candidate explicitly separates it from existing DAG mutation authority"

step S12:
  evidence EV7:
    "Issue 21 treats severity, hard blocking, automatic observation capture, and external integration as future or non-goals, and Candidate 1.0 keeps them out of scope in docs/requirements/plan-review-request-v1.md"

step S13:
  decision D5 based_on EV7:
    "No optional or future feature has been converted into an acceptance blocker, and external synchronization, editor or MCP writes, release, publication, Issue mutation, and plan advance remain out of scope"

step S14:
  evidence EV8:
    "Candidate docs/requirements/plan-review-request-v1.md says creation does not grant plan authority, resolution does not perform a plan change, open requests cannot be orphaned, resolved advance removal is explicit and history-protected, and free text or locators cannot trigger external access"

step S15:
  decision D6 based_on P1, PR1, EV1, EV2, D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, EV8:
    "The independent review is completed and reviewable, with two high-severity contradictions requiring an owner decision and two medium-severity unresolved contract unknowns; the unchanged candidate proceeds to second owner review under REVIEW_THEN_DECIDE, but revision is recommended before acceptance"

step S16:
  pending PD1:
    "Candidate edits, acceptance, specification, ADR, plan mutation, implementation, commit, push, PR, release, publication, Issue mutation, dist-tag changes, and runtime activation remain unauthorized"
